The start report (2eb775ed90) only wrote a log line when it was not
delivered, so a server that took it with a fault reached nobody. Kenneth,
2026-11-16, quoting the proposal back: "My proposal, not built: no dialog,
and a report only when the server answers with a fault and the person has
automatic reports on. Having no network at start stays silent. - go with
your proposal".

Now a server that answers with an HTTP error status is reported through
report_if_automatic, with the status and the server's answer: sent only when
automatic reports are on, and no dialog opens. When nothing answers (no
network, a refused connection, a timeout; the HTTP status is 0) nothing is
reported, and the log line says the start report reached no server. The
decision is launch_failure_report in LaunchRecord, which needs no network.

The HTTP callback runs on the HTTP thread, and report_if_automatic read the
settings from whatever thread called it; AppConfig has no lock. It now moves
to the main thread first, as report_unexpected_error does.

